{"text": "What are the treatments for Aniridia ? How might aniridia be treated? In childhood, treatment for aniridia focuses on regular eye examinations including necessary corrective lenses, tinted lenses to reduce light sensitivity, and occlusion therapy to address vision abnormalities. Children with Wilms tumor-aniridia-genital anomalies-retardation (WAGR) syndrome require regular renal ultrasounds, hearing tests and evaluation by a pediatric oncologist. Additional treatment is adapted to each individual depending on the associated complications.", "source": "NIH Genetic and Rare Diseases Info Center", "citation": "MEDQUAD-2_GARD_QA-0000362-3", "topic": "Aniridia"}
