{"text": "For example, a frequency of 25/25 means that in a study of 25 people all patients were found to have that symptom. Because these frequencies are based on a specific study, the fractions may be different if another group of patients are examined. Sometimes, no information on frequency is available. In these cases, the sign or symptom may be rare or common.", "source": "NIH Genetic and Rare Diseases Info Center", "citation": "MEDQUAD-2_GARD_QA-0000566-1", "topic": "Autosomal dominant optic atrophy and cataract"}
